Programs that exist in order to be programs.

Each of these proves something about being a separate process -- that the
spark loader maps its regions right, that /dev/spark really spawns, that a
stack of arguments arrives, that a spawner waited for an exit status, what an
exec costs. None of them can be a shell builtin: a builtin is not exec'd, so
it would be testing nothing.

Everything a person would actually run is in the shell. These are built when
something is being measured and are not part of the image.

        sh kit/spark kit/probes/tiny /tmp/tiny
